{
 "metric": "fsma_adaptlr_lever",
 "created": "2026-10-15",
 "what": "L3 code lever: decouple the K-shot adaptation LR from the source-training LR. The harness used a single --lr (1e-3) for BOTH source training and K-shot head adaptation; --adapt-lr adds a separate adaptation LR (default = --lr, i.e. the historical coupled behaviour).",
 "why": "Adapting a source-trained head on 5-20 support points at the full source LR over-drifts it. The standard few-shot recipe uses a smaller adaptation LR; the coupled LR was a code-level defect, not a capability ceiling.",
 "honesty_criterion": "Every arm here reuses the SAME frozen source model (same --source-cache-dir), so zero_shot_auc is identical across arms. The claim is therefore stated on the ADAPTED ABSOLUTE AUC (not on the adapted-minus-zero_shot delta), which removes the baseline-illusion failure mode documented in fsma_ep50_lowk_verdict.",
 "protocol": "paper_funnel LOMO, ligand-disjoint; arm=none; head-only; epochs=20; lr=1e-3 (source); adapt_eval_encoder=True (shared by baseline and treatment -> not a confound); metals Ru Ir Rh Os Re; seeds 42,43,44,49,123,7,8,9,10,11; K in {5,10,20}",
 "source_script": "molmetal/scripts/ex1_metal_injection_contrast.py (arm=none, --adapt-lr)",
 "unit": "paired ROC-AUC on the ADAPTED absolute AUC (treatment - baseline), one-sided paired t-test over the same (metal,k,seed) cells",
